Create one production-ready background asset for the Urkaaaz match HUD health
card. This asset will be reused for both BLUE and RED fortress health cards.
Do not create a screen mockup or generate separate team-colored variants.

## Reference inputs

Attach:

1. The latest Urkaaaz match-screen screenshot, to match the actual card scale,
   battlefield palette, and surrounding HUD.
2. The approved match-HUD mockup or reference showing the intended dark,
   restrained metal-and-gold visual language.
3. An approved Urkaaaz Loadout or campaign UI reference, if needed to match
   existing materials and gold edging.

Use the supplied images as visual references only. Do not reproduce their
labels, values, artwork, or complete screen.

## Outputą

- Filename: `health_card_frame.png`
- Source path: `assets_src/match/hud/health_card_frame.png`
- Canvas: exactly 512 x 128 pixels.
- Format: RGBA PNG.
- Produce exactly one standalone asset.

## Design

Create a shallow, horizontal rounded-rectangle health-card panel suitable for
the compact top rail of a landscape mobile game HUD. It should feel like a
polished Urkaaaz interface element: translucent charcoal or blackened iron,
subtle material depth, a fine controlled bronze/gold edge, and a restrained
warm highlight. Keep the treatment clean and readable at small display size.

The panel is shared by both teams. Keep its frame neutral and symmetrical:
do not use blue or red faction coloring, banners, crests, shields, or other
team-specific symbols. Team color is supplied dynamically by the health meter
in Android.

Use a dark, lightly translucent interior surface to support live text and
the health meter over the battlefield. The area inside the frame must remain
visually quiet and unobstructed. Keep the corners and outer edges crisp. Make
the central horizontal area low-detail so it can be stretched without
distorting the corners; do not add nine-patch guide pixels or markers.

## Runtime content — do not bake into the image

The Android HUD renders all of the following dynamically over this asset:

- the `BLUE` or `RED` team label;
- current and maximum fortress HP values;
- the horizontal health meter and its changing fill color;
- accessibility information and any future state indicators.

Do not reserve a pre-drawn colored health bar or include any text, numerals,
icons, symbols, gradients that imply a particular HP percentage, or baked-in
selection/damage state. Do not bake a drop shadow into the PNG; the HUD adds a
soft native shadow programmatically.

## Negative requirements

- No screenshot, mockup, battlefield, fortress, character, scenery, logo,
  watermark, signature, device frame, or contact sheet.
- No blue/red faction variant, crest, shield motif, or team-specific detail.
- No text, numbers, health bar, progress fill, icon, or state indicator.
- No opaque rectangular canvas background: pixels outside the rounded panel
  silhouette must be fully transparent.
- No bulky ornament, spikes, large rivets, bright neon, excessive glow, or
  high-contrast texture that competes with live HP text.
- No uneven corners, asymmetric border, jagged edges, or thin details that
  disappear when rendered at approximately 42 dp high.

## Review checklist

- Confirm the output is one valid 512 x 128 RGBA PNG with the exact filename.
- Confirm the outside of the card silhouette is transparent and the panel
  interior is dark enough for warm ivory text and a blue/red health meter.
- Confirm it works identically for both teams and does not encode an HP value
  or damage state.
- Preview it scaled to the in-game health-card height of approximately 42 dp;
  the border should remain crisp and the center should remain visually quiet.
- Show the asset over both a dark and a bright battlefield crop for review.
  Do not integrate it into Android resources until approved.
